<title>DENMARK: B&amp;O shareholders approve Philips buyback.</title>
<headline>B&amp;O shareholders approve Philips buyback.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders in Danish home entertainments group Bang &amp; Olufsen (B&amp;O) on Tuesday approved the buyback of a 25 percent stake held by Dutch electronics giant Philips, a B&amp;O statement said.</p>
<p>The 540 million crown ($74.6 million) purchase, first announced last month, is to be financed by the issue of 635,000 new B-shares of a nominal 10 crowns each, to be listed on the Copenhagen Stock Exchange on June 26.</p>
<p>The share closed on Tuesday at 415.00 crowns, up 17 from Monday's close.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650 ($ = 7.233 Norwegian Crowns)</p>
